@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il08-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il08-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito-s37-s38-s39-spouse-credits`
IMPORT `ito-s40-children-credit-points`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for ss 37, 38, 39 and 40(b). Row IL-08.
--
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the text quoted in the rule modules (NOTES.md
-- section 5), before the rules were run. None has been edited to match the code. A failing
-- assertion is a finding. The value of a credit point for s 38(b) is 2,904 for 2026 (row IL-01's
-- published 2025 figure, frozen for 2025-2027 by s 120B(e)(1): row IL-07's fork K2).
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — sections 37, 38, 39 and 40(b)`

§§ `Section 40(b) — the people`

-- A child, seen from the parent asked about. Each helper fixes the facts its name states.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A child, for section 40(b)`
`a child living with and maintained by its single father, born in` `the year` MEANS
    `A child, for section 40(b)` WITH
        `tax year of birth`                                                                IS `the year`
        `the parent is`                                                                    IS `the father of the child`
        `the parent maintained the child`                                                  IS TRUE
        `the child is with the parent`                                                     IS TRUE
        `in a single-parent family`                                                        IS TRUE
        `the other parent died in or before the tax year`                                  IS FALSE
        `registered in the population register without the details of one parent`          IS FALSE
        `the mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS FALSE
        `the other parent is an Israeli resident in the tax year`                          IS TRUE
        `the other parent has credit points for the child under paragraph (1)`             IS FALSE

GIVEN `the year`  IS A NUMBER
      `elects`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A child, for section 40(b)`
`a child living with and maintained by its single mother, born in` `the year` `, the mother electing under (1A1):` `elects` MEANS
    `A child, for section 40(b)` WITH
        `tax year of birth`                                                                IS `the year`
        `the parent is`                                                                    IS `the mother of the child`
        `the parent maintained the child`                                                  IS TRUE
        `the child is with the parent`                                                     IS TRUE
        `in a single-parent family`                                                        IS TRUE
        `the other parent died in or before the tax year`                                  IS FALSE
        `registered in the population register without the details of one parent`          IS FALSE
        `the mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS `elects`
        `the other parent is an Israeli resident in the tax year`                          IS TRUE
        `the other parent has credit points for the child under paragraph (1)`             IS FALSE

-- Seen from a father the child does not live with; the facts about the mother as given.
GIVEN `the year`                       IS A NUMBER
      `the mother is resident`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mother has (1) points`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A child, for section 40(b)`
`a child not living with its father, born in` `the year` `; the mother resident:` `the mother is resident` `, with paragraph (1) points:` `the mother has (1) points` MEANS
    `A child, for section 40(b)` WITH
        `tax year of birth`                                                                IS `the year`
        `the parent is`                                                                    IS `the father of the child`
        `the parent maintained the child`                                                  IS FALSE
        `the child is with the parent`                                                     IS FALSE
        `in a single-parent family`                                                        IS TRUE
        `the other parent died in or before the tax year`                                  IS FALSE
        `registered in the population register without the details of one parent`          IS FALSE
        `the mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS FALSE
        `the other parent is an Israeli resident in the tax year`                          IS `the mother is resident`
        `the other parent has credit points for the child under paragraph (1)`             IS `the mother has (1) points`

-- Seen from a mother the child does not live with either; the father is resident, without (1) points.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A child, for section 40(b)`
`a child living with neither parent, seen from its mother, born in` `the year` MEANS
    `A child, for section 40(b)` WITH
        `tax year of birth`                                                                IS `the year`
        `the parent is`                                                                    IS `the mother of the child`
        `the parent maintained the child`                                                  IS TRUE
        `the child is with the parent`                                                     IS FALSE
        `in a single-parent family`                                                        IS TRUE
        `the other parent died in or before the tax year`                                  IS FALSE
        `registered in the population register without the details of one parent`          IS FALSE
        `the mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS FALSE
        `the other parent is an Israeli resident in the tax year`                          IS TRUE
        `the other parent has credit points for the child under paragraph (1)`             IS FALSE

-- A child of one parent: the father died.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A child, for section 40(b)`
`a child whose father has died, living with and maintained by its mother, born in` `the year` MEANS
    `A child, for section 40(b)` WITH
        `tax year of birth`                                                                IS `the year`
        `the parent is`                                                                    IS `the mother of the child`
        `the parent maintained the child`                                                  IS TRUE
        `the child is with the parent`                                                     IS TRUE
        `in a single-parent family`                                                        IS TRUE
        `the other parent died in or before the tax year`                                  IS TRUE
        `registered in the population register without the details of one parent`          IS FALSE
        `the mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS FALSE
        `the other parent is an Israeli resident in the tax year`                          IS FALSE
        `the other parent has credit points for the child under paragraph (1)`             IS FALSE

-- The parent.
GIVEN `the year`            IS A NUMBER
      `resident`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `single-parent`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 37`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `apart`               IS A BOOLEAN
      `share`               IS A NUMBER
      `foreign worker`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `the children`        IS A LIST OF `A child, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
`a parent in` `the year` `, resident:` `resident` `, in a single-parent family:` `single-parent` `, with a s 37 point:` `s 37` `, living apart:` `apart` `, bearing a share of` `share` `, a foreign worker:` `foreign worker` `, with children` `the children` MEANS
    `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)` WITH
        `tax year`                                    IS `the year`
        `an Israeli resident in the tax year`         IS `resident`
        `a parent in a single-parent family`          IS `single-parent`
        `entitled to a credit point under section 37` IS `s 37`
        `living apart from the other parent`          IS `apart`
        `share of the children's maintenance expenses borne` IS `share`
        `a foreign worker`                            IS `foreign worker`
        `children`                                    IS `the children`

GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`all the s 40(b) points of` p MEANS
         `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax generally, for` p
    PLUS `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` p

§§ `Section 40(b)(1) and (2) — the parent the children live with`

-- Version 0.5.0 (fork F16, SHRUG): the further point of (1B) and (2) is given once, or once for each
-- child, and by default declined where that decides. The tests below with two children and a further
-- point were written on "once" (versions 0.1.0 to 0.4.0); they now ask it by name, values unchanged.
`the further point once` MEANS
    `The readings of section 40(b)` WITH
        `paragraph (1A), not entitled under paragraph (1)` IS `declined where the reading of paragraph (1A) decides`
        `paragraphs (1B) and (2), one further point`       IS `once`

-- SP1, row IL-07's household H12: a single father in 2026 with children born 2015 and 2019 (turning
-- 11 and 7), who live with him and whom he maintains, living apart from their mother, who pays
-- nothing. (1): 2 + 2 = 4. (2): one more point, being entitled under (1). Against the tax generally 5;
-- nothing set against the tax on income from personal exertion.
`SP1` MEANS `a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child living with and maintained by its single father, born in` 2015), (`a child living with and maintained by its single father, born in` 2019))
#ASSERT (`the credit points under section 40(b) for` `SP1`)'s `under paragraph (1), with the election of (1A1)` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT (`the credit points under section 40(b) for` `SP1` `, reading section 40(b) as` `the further point once`)'s `under paragraph (2)` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax generally, for` `SP1` `, reading section 40(b) as` `the further point once` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` `SP1` EQUALS 0
-- Not living apart from the other parent: (2) gives nothing, 4.
#ASSERT `all the s 40(b) points of` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` FALSE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child living with and maintained by its single father, born in` 2015), (`a child living with and maintained by its single father, born in` 2019))) EQUALS 4

-- SP2: a single mother in 2026, a child born 2026 and one born 2023 (turning 0 and 3).
-- Without the election: 2.5 + 3.5 = 6, and 1 under (2): 7.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) in all, for` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child living with and maintained by its single mother, born in` 2026 `, the mother electing under (1A1):` FALSE), (`a child living with and maintained by its single mother, born in` 2023 `, the mother electing under (1A1):` FALSE))) `, reading section 40(b) as` `the further point once` EQUALS 7
-- Electing under (1A1) for the newborn: 1.5 + 3.5 + 1 = 6 in 2026 ...
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) in all, for` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child living with and maintained by its single mother, born in` 2026 `, the mother electing under (1A1):` TRUE), (`a child living with and maintained by its single mother, born in` 2023 `, the mother electing under (1A1):` FALSE))) `, reading section 40(b) as` `the further point once` EQUALS 6
-- ... and in 2027 the children turn 1 and 4: 4.5 + 1 = 5.5 and 2.5, and 1 under (2): 9.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) in all, for` (`a parent in` 2027 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child living with and maintained by its single mother, born in` 2026 `, the mother electing under (1A1):` TRUE), (`a child living with and maintained by its single mother, born in` 2023 `, the mother electing under (1A1):` FALSE))) `, reading section 40(b) as` `the further point once` EQUALS 9

-- The year of majority and after: a child turning 18 gives 1/2 under (1); turning 19, nothing.
#ASSERT `all the s 40(b) points of` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` FALSE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child living with and maintained by its single mother, born in` 2008 `, the mother electing under (1A1):` FALSE))) EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `all the s 40(b) points of` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` FALSE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child living with and maintained by its single mother, born in` 2007 `, the mother electing under (1A1):` FALSE))) EQUALS 0

-- The parent's own limbs: not resident, or entitled to a s 37 point, gives nothing under (1).
#ASSERT `all the s 40(b) points of` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` FALSE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child living with and maintained by its single father, born in` 2015))) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `all the s 40(b) points of` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` TRUE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child living with and maintained by its single father, born in` 2015))) EQUALS 0
-- Not "a parent in a single-parent family": nothing under (1).
#ASSERT `all the s 40(b) points of` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` FALSE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` FALSE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child living with and maintained by its single father, born in` 2015))) EQUALS 0

§§ `Section 40(b)(1A) and (2) — the parent the children do not live with`

-- SP3: their father in 2026, resident, not living with the children (born 2015 and 2019), who live
-- with their mother, a resident with points for them under (1). (1A): the man's table, 1 + 1 = 2,
-- against the tax on his income from personal exertion. (2): the parents live apart and he bears 30%
-- of the maintenance: 0.3 of a point, against the tax generally.
`SP3` MEANS `a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` FALSE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 0.3 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child not living with its father, born in` 2015 `; the mother resident:` TRUE `, with paragraph (1) points:` TRUE), (`a child not living with its father, born in` 2019 `; the mother resident:` TRUE `, with paragraph (1) points:` TRUE))
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` `SP3` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax generally, for` `SP3` EQUALS 0.3
-- A child of 3 and one of 18: (1A) gives 3.5 and nothing (no row for the year of majority).
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` FALSE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child not living with its father, born in` 2023 `; the mother resident:` TRUE `, with paragraph (1) points:` TRUE), (`a child not living with its father, born in` 2008 `; the mother resident:` TRUE `, with paragraph (1) points:` TRUE))) EQUALS 3.5

-- SP4: as SP3, but the mother, a resident, has no points for the children under (1). The proviso
-- moves the (1A) points to her: the father has none.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` FALSE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child not living with its father, born in` 2015 `; the mother resident:` TRUE `, with paragraph (1) points:` FALSE), (`a child not living with its father, born in` 2019 `; the mother resident:` TRUE `, with paragraph (1) points:` FALSE))) EQUALS 0
-- ... and the mother, asked about, has them: 1 + 1 = 2.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child living with neither parent, seen from its mother, born in` 2015), (`a child living with neither parent, seen from its mother, born in` 2019))) EQUALS 2
-- If the mother were not a resident, the proviso would not move them: the father keeps 2.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` FALSE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child not living with its father, born in` 2015 `; the mother resident:` FALSE `, with paragraph (1) points:` FALSE), (`a child not living with its father, born in` 2019 `; the mother resident:` FALSE `, with paragraph (1) points:` FALSE))) EQUALS 2

-- Version 0.3.0 (O1, the capstone's second independent pass). (2)'s second limb needs the
-- maintenance "divided between them": a share of 1 (or 0) is not divided, and gives nothing.
-- O1: a father not resident, not in a single-parent family, living apart, bearing all the
-- maintenance of a child born 2016 who lives with its mother abroad, she having no (1) points: nothing
-- under (2) (version 0.1.0: 1), and nothing under (1A), which is for a resident.
#ASSERT `all the s 40(b) points of` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` FALSE `, in a single-parent family:` FALSE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 1 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child not living with its father, born in` 2016 `; the mother resident:` FALSE `, with paragraph (1) points:` FALSE))) EQUALS 0
-- SP3's father bearing all of it: nothing under (2) (version 0.1.0: 1); his (1A) point stays.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax generally, for` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` FALSE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 1 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child not living with its father, born in` 2016 `; the mother resident:` TRUE `, with paragraph (1) points:` TRUE))) EQUALS 0
-- A father not resident bearing 30%, the mother resident with (1) points: whether (2) credits a
-- non-resident the text does not say (fork F18, declined from 0.3.0; versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0: 0.3).
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax generally, for` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` FALSE `, in a single-parent family:` FALSE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 0.3 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child not living with its father, born in` 2016 `; the mother resident:` TRUE `, with paragraph (1) points:` TRUE))) BECAUSE "section 40(b)(2) does not say whether its point for a share of the maintenance goes to a parent who is not an Israeli resident"
-- A resident father bearing 30%, the mother abroad with no (1) points: neither parent is entitled under
-- (1), and whether the second limb then reaches him the text does not say (fork F37; version 0.1.0: 0.3).
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax generally, for` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` FALSE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 0.3 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child not living with its father, born in` 2016 `; the mother resident:` FALSE `, with paragraph (1) points:` FALSE))) BECAUSE "section 40(b)(2) does not say whether its point for a share of the maintenance goes to a parent where the other parent is not entitled under paragraph (1) either"

§§ `Section 40(b)(1B) — a child of one parent`

-- SP5: a widowed mother in 2026 with a child born 2021 (turning 5). (1): 2.5. (1B): one further
-- point and the (1A) table's 2.5 for the child, 3.5 against the tax on income from personal
-- exertion. (2): the parents do not "live apart"; nothing.
`SP5` MEANS `a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` FALSE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child whose father has died, living with and maintained by its mother, born in` 2021))
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax generally, for` `SP5` EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` `SP5` EQUALS 3.5
-- Two such children, turning 5 and 9: (1) 2.5 + 2; (1B) one point once, and 2.5 + 1: 4.5.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` FALSE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child whose father has died, living with and maintained by its mother, born in` 2021), (`a child whose father has died, living with and maintained by its mother, born in` 2017))) `, reading section 40(b) as` `the further point once` EQUALS 4.5
#ASSERT `s 40(b)(3) — a child of one parent, in tax year` 2026 `:` ((`a child whose father has died, living with and maintained by its mother, born in` 2021))
#ASSERT NOT `s 40(b)(3) — a child of one parent, in tax year` 2026 `:` ((`a child whose father has died, living with and maintained by its mother, born in` 2007))

-- Version 0.2.0 (OB1): (1A1) moves one point, not two, for a child of one parent. SP6: a widowed
-- mother whose child was born in 2025, she electing under (1A1).
-- 2025 (the year of birth, age 0): (1) 2.5 less the one point moved = 1.5, against the tax generally;
-- (1B) one point and the (1A) table's 2.5 = 3.5, against the tax on income from personal exertion;
-- 5 in all (6 without the election; version 0.1.0 gave 4, moving a second point out of the 2.5).
-- 2026 (age 1): (1) 4.5 plus the point moved = 5.5; (1B) 1 + 4.5 = 5.5; 11 in all (10 without the
-- election; version 0.1.0 gave 12).
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `elects`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A child, for section 40(b)`
`a child of one parent, its father dead, with its mother, born in` `the year` `, she electing under (1A1):` `elects` MEANS
    `A child, for section 40(b)` WITH
        `tax year of birth`                                                                IS `the year`
        `the parent is`                                                                    IS `the mother of the child`
        `the parent maintained the child`                                                  IS TRUE
        `the child is with the parent`                                                     IS TRUE
        `in a single-parent family`                                                        IS TRUE
        `the other parent died in or before the tax year`                                  IS TRUE
        `registered in the population register without the details of one parent`          IS FALSE
        `the mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS `elects`
        `the other parent is an Israeli resident in the tax year`                          IS FALSE
        `the other parent has credit points for the child under paragraph (1)`             IS FALSE

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `elects`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
`SP6 in` `the year` `, electing:` `elects` MEANS
    `a parent in` `the year` `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` FALSE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child of one parent, its father dead, with its mother, born in` 2025 `, she electing under (1A1):` `elects`))

#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax generally, for` (`SP6 in` 2025 `, electing:` TRUE) EQUALS 1.5
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` (`SP6 in` 2025 `, electing:` TRUE) EQUALS 3.5
#ASSERT `all the s 40(b) points of` (`SP6 in` 2025 `, electing:` TRUE) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `all the s 40(b) points of` (`SP6 in` 2025 `, electing:` FALSE) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax generally, for` (`SP6 in` 2026 `, electing:` TRUE) EQUALS 5.5
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` (`SP6 in` 2026 `, electing:` TRUE) EQUALS 5.5
#ASSERT `all the s 40(b) points of` (`SP6 in` 2026 `, electing:` TRUE) EQUALS 11
#ASSERT `all the s 40(b) points of` (`SP6 in` 2026 `, electing:` FALSE) EQUALS 10

§§ `Section 40(b) — forks F15 and F16 as switches (version 0.5.0, SHRUG)`

`the further point for each child` MEANS
    `The readings of section 40(b)` WITH
        `paragraph (1A), not entitled under paragraph (1)` IS `declined where the reading of paragraph (1A) decides`
        `paragraphs (1B) and (2), one further point`       IS `once for each child`
`(1A) for that child` MEANS
    `The readings of section 40(b)` WITH
        `paragraph (1A), not entitled under paragraph (1)` IS `for that child`
        `paragraphs (1B) and (2), one further point`       IS `declined where the reading of paragraphs (1B) and (2) decides`
`(1A) for any child` MEANS
    `The readings of section 40(b)` WITH
        `paragraph (1A), not entitled under paragraph (1)` IS `for any child`
        `paragraphs (1B) and (2), one further point`       IS `declined where the reading of paragraphs (1B) and (2) decides`

-- The switches name the defaults.
#ASSERT (`section 40(b) — the readings this row takes`)'s `paragraph (1A), not entitled under paragraph (1)` EQUALS `declined where the reading of paragraph (1A) decides`
#ASSERT (`section 40(b) — the readings this row takes`)'s `paragraphs (1B) and (2), one further point` EQUALS `declined where the reading of paragraphs (1B) and (2) decides`

-- F16 under (2): SP1, two children with him, living apart. Once: (2) 1, against the tax generally
-- 4 + 1 = 5 (above). For each child: (2) 2, generally 6. By default declined.
#ASSERT (`the credit points under section 40(b) for` `SP1` `, reading section 40(b) as` `the further point for each child`)'s `under paragraph (2)` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax generally, for` `SP1` `, reading section 40(b) as` `the further point for each child` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax generally, for` `SP1` BECAUSE "section 40(b)(1B) and (2) do not say whether the one further credit point is given once or for each child, and here it decides"
-- What F16 does not touch is answered by default: SP1's points under (1), 4, and against the tax on
-- income from personal exertion, 0.
#ASSERT (`the credit points under section 40(b) for` `SP1`)'s `under paragraph (1), with the election of (1A1)` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` `SP1` EQUALS 0

-- F16 under (1B): a widowed mother with two children of one parent, turning 5 and 9. Once: 1 + 2.5 + 1
-- = 4.5 against the tax on income from personal exertion (above); for each child: 2 + 2.5 + 1 = 5.5;
-- in all, with (1)'s 2.5 + 2: 9 or 10. By default declined.
`SP7` MEANS `a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` FALSE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child whose father has died, living with and maintained by its mother, born in` 2021), (`a child whose father has died, living with and maintained by its mother, born in` 2017))
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` `SP7` `, reading section 40(b) as` `the further point for each child` EQUALS 5.5
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) in all, for` `SP7` `, reading section 40(b) as` `the further point once` EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) in all, for` `SP7` `, reading section 40(b) as` `the further point for each child` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40(b) in all, for` `SP7` BECAUSE "section 40(b)(1B) and (2) do not say whether the one further credit point is given once or for each child, and here it decides"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax generally, for` `SP7` EQUALS 4.5

-- F15, asked about the father: a single father with a child born 2015 who lives with him (2 points
-- under (1)), and a child born 2019 in a single-parent family who lives with its mother, a resident
-- with (1) points for it. For that child, he is not entitled under (1) for the second child: (1A)'s
-- 1 point (age 7). For any child, he is entitled under (1), for the first: none. By default declined;
-- his points under (1), 2, are answered.
`SP8` MEANS `a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` FALSE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child living with and maintained by its single father, born in` 2015), (`a child not living with its father, born in` 2019 `; the mother resident:` TRUE `, with paragraph (1) points:` TRUE))
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` `SP8` `, reading section 40(b) as` `(1A) for that child` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` `SP8` `, reading section 40(b) as` `(1A) for any child` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` `SP8` BECAUSE "section 40(b)(1A) does not say whether the father is to be not entitled under paragraph (1) for that child or for any child, and here it decides"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax generally, for` `SP8` EQUALS 2
-- A father with only the child who lives with its mother (SP3's first child): both readings give (1A)'s
-- 1 point, answered by default.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` FALSE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` FALSE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child not living with its father, born in` 2019 `; the mother resident:` TRUE `, with paragraph (1) points:` TRUE))) EQUALS 1

-- F15, asked about the mother (the proviso): a resident mother with a child born 2019 who lives with
-- neither parent, the father resident without (1) points for it, and a child born 2015 who lives with
-- the father, who has (1) points for it. For that child: the father is not entitled under (1) for the
-- first, and (1A)'s 1 point goes to her. For any child (read from the children on her record): he is
-- entitled, for the second, and none goes to her. By default declined.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A child, for section 40(b)`
`a child living with its father, who has paragraph (1) points for it, seen from its mother, born in` `the year` MEANS
    `A child, for section 40(b)` WITH
        `tax year of birth`                                                                IS `the year`
        `the parent is`                                                                    IS `the mother of the child`
        `the parent maintained the child`                                                  IS FALSE
        `the child is with the parent`                                                     IS FALSE
        `in a single-parent family`                                                        IS TRUE
        `the other parent died in or before the tax year`                                  IS FALSE
        `registered in the population register without the details of one parent`          IS FALSE
        `the mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS FALSE
        `the other parent is an Israeli resident in the tax year`                          IS TRUE
        `the other parent has credit points for the child under paragraph (1)`             IS TRUE
`SP9` MEANS `a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` FALSE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child living with neither parent, seen from its mother, born in` 2019), (`a child living with its father, who has paragraph (1) points for it, seen from its mother, born in` 2015))
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` `SP9` `, reading section 40(b) as` `(1A) for that child` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` `SP9` `, reading section 40(b) as` `(1A) for any child` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` `SP9` BECAUSE "section 40(b)(1A) does not say whether the father is to be not entitled under paragraph (1) for that child or for any child, and here it decides"

§§ `Section 40(b) — tax years and section 48A`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40(b) for` (`a parent in` 2023 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` FALSE `, with children` (LIST (`a child living with and maintained by its single father, born in` 2015))) BECAUSE "row IL-08 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40(b) for` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` TRUE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` TRUE `, with children` (LIST (`a child living with and maintained by its single father, born in` 2015))) BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT `all the s 40(b) points of` (`a parent in` 2026 `, resident:` FALSE `, in a single-parent family:` TRUE `, with a s 37 point:` FALSE `, living apart:` FALSE `, bearing a share of` 0 `, a foreign worker:` TRUE `, with children` (LIST (`a child living with and maintained by its single father, born in` 2015))) EQUALS 0

§§ `Sections 37, 38 and 39 — the people`

-- Positional, under this ruler (the order of the DECLARE in ito-il08-nouns.l4):
--  1 tax year | 2 resident | 3 has a spouse | 4 he reached retirement age | 5 spouse reached it |
--  6 he is blind/disabled | 7 spouse is | 8 maintenance proved | 9 registered spouse |
-- 10 income includes spouse's | 11 spouse's income from exertion proved | 12 spouse's taxable income |
-- 13 allowance points | 14 spouse helped | 15 the s 39 election (0.3.0: three-way) | 16 Area resident, not citizen | 17 foreign worker
`R, a resident whose spouse he maintains, past retirement age` MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` OF 2026, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, `made no election`, FALSE, FALSE
`R, maintenance not proved` MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` OF 2026, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, `made no election`, FALSE, FALSE
`B, whose spouse is blind, maintenance proved` MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` OF 2026, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, `made no election`, FALSE, FALSE
`Y, not a beneficiary individual, maintenance proved` MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` OF 2026, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, `made no election`, FALSE, FALSE
`N, R but not resident` MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` OF 2026, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, `made no election`, FALSE, FALSE
`A, R but a non-resident Area resident, not a citizen` MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` OF 2026, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, `made no election`, TRUE, FALSE
`F, R but a foreign worker` MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` OF 2026, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, `made no election`, FALSE, TRUE
`U, past retirement age with no spouse` MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` OF 2026, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, `made no election`, FALSE, FALSE

-- s 38: a registered spouse whose income includes the working spouse's, proved to be from exertion.
GIVEN `spouse's income`   IS A NUMBER
      `allowance points`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `spouse past retirement age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `maintenance proved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `spouse helped`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the s 39 election` IS A `The election under section 39 between sections 38 and 39`
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
`a registered spouse in 2026 whose spouse earned` `spouse's income` `, allowance points:` `allowance points` `, spouse past retirement age:` `spouse past retirement age` `, maintenance proved:` `maintenance proved` `, spouse helped in the business:` `spouse helped` `, the s 39 election:` `the s 39 election` MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` OF 2026, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, `spouse past retirement age`, FALSE, FALSE, `maintenance proved`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `spouse's income`, `allowance points`, `spouse helped`, `the s 39 election`, FALSE, FALSE

§§ `Section 37`

#ASSERT `the credit points under section 37 for` `R, a resident whose spouse he maintains, past retirement age` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 37 for` `R, maintenance not proved` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 37 for` `B, whose spouse is blind, maintenance proved` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 37 for` `Y, not a beneficiary individual, maintenance proved` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 37 for` `N, R but not resident` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 37 for` `U, past retirement age with no spouse` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 37 for` `A, R but a non-resident Area resident, not a citizen` BECAUSE "section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 37 for` `F, R but a foreign worker` BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 37 for` (`An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` OF 2023, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, `made no election`, FALSE, FALSE) BECAUSE "row IL-08 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024"

§§ `Section 38`

-- 1/4 + 1 1/2 = 1.75; with allowance points 1/4 + 1 3/4 = 2.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`a registered spouse in 2026 whose spouse earned` 100000 `, allowance points:` FALSE `, spouse past retirement age:` FALSE `, maintenance proved:` FALSE `, spouse helped in the business:` FALSE `, the s 39 election:` `made no election`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 1.75
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`a registered spouse in 2026 whose spouse earned` 100000 `, allowance points:` TRUE `, spouse past retirement age:` FALSE `, maintenance proved:` FALSE `, spouse helped in the business:` FALSE `, the s 39 election:` `made no election`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 2
-- A beneficiary individual (the spouse is past retirement age) also has s 37's point: 2.75.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`a registered spouse in 2026 whose spouse earned` 100000 `, allowance points:` FALSE `, spouse past retirement age:` TRUE `, maintenance proved:` FALSE `, spouse helped in the business:` FALSE `, the s 39 election:` `made no election`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 2.75
-- (b): five times 1.75 points at 2,904 is 25,410. A spouse earning 25,410 is left out and the points
-- go; one earning 25,411 is not.
#ASSERT `s 38(b) — five times the amount of the said parts of credit points, for` (`a registered spouse in 2026 whose spouse earned` 25410 `, allowance points:` FALSE `, spouse past retirement age:` FALSE `, maintenance proved:` FALSE `, spouse helped in the business:` FALSE `, the s 39 election:` `made no election`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 25410
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`a registered spouse in 2026 whose spouse earned` 25410 `, allowance points:` FALSE `, spouse past retirement age:` FALSE `, maintenance proved:` FALSE `, spouse helped in the business:` FALSE `, the s 39 election:` `made no election`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`a registered spouse in 2026 whose spouse earned` 25411 `, allowance points:` FALSE `, spouse past retirement age:` FALSE `, maintenance proved:` FALSE `, spouse helped in the business:` FALSE `, the s 39 election:` `made no election`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 1.75
-- With allowance points the bar is five times 2 points: 29,040.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`a registered spouse in 2026 whose spouse earned` 29040 `, allowance points:` TRUE `, spouse past retirement age:` FALSE `, maintenance proved:` FALSE `, spouse helped in the business:` FALSE `, the s 39 election:` `made no election`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 0
-- Not the registered spouse, or the spouse's income not proved to be from exertion: nothing.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` OF 2026, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 100000, FALSE, FALSE, `made no election`, FALSE, FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 for` (`An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` OF 2026, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 100000, FALSE, FALSE, `made no election`, FALSE, FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 0

§§ `Section 39, and the three together`

-- The spouse helped in the business: 1 1/2; a beneficiary individual, 2 1/2.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39 for` (`An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` OF 2026, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, TRUE, `made no election`, FALSE, FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 1.5
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39 for` (`An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` OF 2026, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, TRUE, `made no election`, FALSE, FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 2.5
-- Entitled under both ss 38 and 39: the credits of one, at his choice. Electing s 38: s 38's 1.75
-- (version 0.1.0: "not electing s 39", a boolean FALSE; from 0.3.0 the election is three-way, D109).
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 37, 38 and 39 for` (`a registered spouse in 2026 whose spouse earned` 100000 `, allowance points:` FALSE `, spouse past retirement age:` FALSE `, maintenance proved:` FALSE `, spouse helped in the business:` TRUE `, the s 39 election:` `elected the credits of section 38`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 1.75
-- Electing s 39: 1.5.
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 37, 38 and 39 for` (`a registered spouse in 2026 whose spouse earned` 100000 `, allowance points:` FALSE `, spouse past retirement age:` FALSE `, maintenance proved:` FALSE `, spouse helped in the business:` TRUE `, the s 39 election:` `elected the credits of section 39`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 1.5
-- s 37 on its own terms and s 38's "also the point under s 37": counted once. The spouse past
-- retirement age, maintenance proved, income 100,000: 1 (s 37) + 2.75 (s 38) - 1 = 2.75.
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 37, 38 and 39 for` (`a registered spouse in 2026 whose spouse earned` 100000 `, allowance points:` FALSE `, spouse past retirement age:` TRUE `, maintenance proved:` TRUE `, spouse helped in the business:` FALSE `, the s 39 election:` `made no election`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 2.75
-- s 37 alone: 1.
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 37, 38 and 39 for` `R, a resident whose spouse he maintains, past retirement age` `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 1
-- A foreign worker credited under s 39: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 39 for` (`An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` OF 2026, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, TRUE, `made no election`, FALSE, TRUE) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"

§§ `Section 39's election, as a three-way input (version 0.2.0, D109; in the record from 0.3.0)`

-- Entitled under both ss 38 and 39 (registered spouse, spouse's income 100,000 from exertion, and the
-- spouse helped in the business): "the credits under one of the two sections, at his choice". With no
-- choice made the text gives no answer: declined, by each of the three rules that read the election.
-- Electing s 38: 1/4 + 1 1/2 = 1.75 and s 39 nothing; electing s 39: 1 1/2 and s 38 nothing (above).
GIVEN e IS A `The election under section 39 between sections 38 and 39`
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39`
`D, entitled under both ss 38 and 39, the s 39 election:` e MEANS
    `a registered spouse in 2026 whose spouse earned` 100000 `, allowance points:` FALSE `, spouse past retirement age:` FALSE `, maintenance proved:` FALSE `, spouse helped in the business:` TRUE `, the s 39 election:` e
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under sections 37, 38 and 39 for` (`D, entitled under both ss 38 and 39, the s 39 election:` `made no election`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 BECAUSE "section 39 gives the credits of one of sections 38 and 39, at the individual's choice, and no choice has been made"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 39 for` (`D, entitled under both ss 38 and 39, the s 39 election:` `made no election`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 BECAUSE "section 39 gives the credits of one of sections 38 and 39, at the individual's choice, and no choice has been made"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 38 after the election under section 39, for` (`D, entitled under both ss 38 and 39, the s 39 election:` `made no election`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 BECAUSE "section 39 gives the credits of one of sections 38 and 39, at the individual's choice, and no choice has been made"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 after the election under section 39, for` (`D, entitled under both ss 38 and 39, the s 39 election:` `elected the credits of section 38`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 1.75
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39 for` (`D, entitled under both ss 38 and 39, the s 39 election:` `elected the credits of section 38`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39 for` (`D, entitled under both ss 38 and 39, the s 39 election:` `elected the credits of section 39`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 1.5
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 38 after the election under section 39, for` (`D, entitled under both ss 38 and 39, the s 39 election:` `elected the credits of section 39`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 0
-- Where only one section applies, there is nothing to choose and the election is not read: s 38 alone
-- (the spouse did not help) 1.75; s 39 alone (not the registered spouse) 1.5; neither election made.
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 37, 38 and 39 for` (`a registered spouse in 2026 whose spouse earned` 100000 `, allowance points:` FALSE `, spouse past retirement age:` FALSE `, maintenance proved:` FALSE `, spouse helped in the business:` FALSE `, the s 39 election:` `made no election`) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 1.75
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 37, 38 and 39 for` (`An individual in a tax year, for sections 37 to 39` OF 2026, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, TRUE, `made no election`, FALSE, FALSE) `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 1.5
